# seal-os unsafe-code audit fixture - version 1
#
# Scan algorithm (the host checker and the kernel-side parser must agree
# exactly, or the gate is measuring two different things):
#   1. Walk kernel/seal-os/src recursively; take every file ending in ".rs".
#      Paths are relative to kernel/seal-os/src, "/" separated, sorted
#      lexicographically by directory then filename.
#   2. Split each file on '\n'. For each line, count occurrences of the exact
#      substring "unsafe {". That count is the line's unsafe-block sites.
#      `unsafe fn`, `unsafe impl`, `unsafe trait` and `unsafe extern` declare
#      unsafety rather than perform it and are not counted as blocks.
#   3. A site is JUSTIFIED when the substring "SAFETY:" appears on that same
#      line, or anywhere in the contiguous run of comment lines directly above
#      it - walk upward while the trimmed line starts with "//" and stop at the
#      first line that does not. Otherwise the site is UNJUSTIFIED.
#   4. Only files with at least one site are listed below.
#
# Gate contract:
#   total        must equal the re-scanned total exactly - no silent drift.
#   unjustified  must be <= the value below. It may only ratchet down.
#   Per file the recorded justified count is a floor and the implied
#   unjustified count is a ceiling: a listed file that gains an unjustified
#   block fails, and an unlisted file that gains any unjustified block fails.
#
# Finding. Before this audit existed the tree held 573 unsafe blocks, of which
# 5 carried a SAFETY justification and 568 did not - 99.1% undocumented. The
# audit code itself contributed 4 further blocks, all justified. The subsystems
# that landed alongside it - atlas, bundle, the GCN assembler, the GPU bench and
# the filesystem parity harness - contributed a further 17, none justified, so
# the totals below now read 594 / 9 / 585. The unjustified count is the real
# number and it is not rounded: 98.5% of the unsafe blocks in this kernel have
# no written justification. The gate freezes that count so it can only fall.
#
# That the number went UP by 17 in the same change that introduced the gate is
# the honest reading: the ratchet stops the next regression, it does not undo
# this one. Justifications get written when those files are next touched.
#
# Regenerate: re-run the algorithm above over kernel/seal-os/src. Any change to
# the numbers is a deliberate edit to this file and shows up in review.
#
# Format: "file <relpath> <sites> <justified>"
version 1
